Everything under this directory comes from the Human Development Report
statistics of the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), published by
its Human Development Report Office (HDRO) at
https://hdr.undp.org/data-center/documentation-and-downloads. The global
Multidimensional Poverty Index tables are produced jointly by HDRO and the
Oxford Poverty and Human Development Initiative (OPHI), University of
Oxford.

The Terms of use of hdr.undp.org (https://hdr.undp.org/terms-use, read on
2026-10-04) say: "All materials provided on this website are copyrighted
under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO license." They require
appropriate credit, a link to the licence, an indication of where changes
were made, and no suggestion that the licensor endorses the user or the
use. The data files carry no licence text of their own.

Recommended citation (metadata workbook, sheet recommended_citation):
Source: UNDP (United Nations Development Programme). 2025. Human Development
Report 2025 - A matter of choice: People and possibilities in the age of AI.
New York.

HDRO recalculates the entire series of HDI values and ranks every year with
the most recent revised data, so values and ranks from different reports
cannot be compared directly.

This dataset is not made or endorsed by UNDP or HDRO.

The files under raw/<release>/ are HDRO's own, byte for byte; each
release's MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and
Last-Modified.

The Parquet under parquet/<release>/ was made from the composite indices
time series CSV:

  - the CSV was decoded from Windows-1252 and its text written as UTF-8
  - columns were typed by name: iso3, country, hdicode and region as text;
    hdi_rank, gii_rank, gdi_group and rankdiff_hdi_phdi as integers; the
    other indicators of the codebook as floating-point numbers; an empty
    cell as NULL
  - composite_indices.parquet keeps the CSV's 206 rows and 1,112 columns in
    their order
  - composite_indices_long.parquet holds the same values one per row
    (iso3, country, region, indicator, year, value), indicator and year
    taken from the column name <indicator>_<year>; empty cells are left
    out, and rows are sorted by indicator, iso3 and year
  - no value was changed

The statistical annex workbooks and the metadata workbook are not
converted.

The code that fetches, checks and converts is in the repository this
dataset was built from and does not apply here.
